        <param name="events">The list of events to add. This value cannot be null.</param>
        <summary>Adds a list of existing Events to the composition.</summary>
        <returns>This Builder object. This value cannot be null.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Adds a list of existing Events to the composition.</para>
          <para>For example, if an event within the list has a start time of 50ms, and startTimeShiftMillis is 100ms, the event will be shifted to start at 150ms within this builder's timeline.</para>
          <para>All events will be added and validated according to the builder's timing rules, with best-effort checks to prevent overlaps being introduced by the shift.</para>
          <para>You can get events by calling VibrationEffect.getEvents() on non-repeating effects.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/VibrationEffect.Builder#addEvents(long,%20java.util.List&lt;android.os.VibrationEffect.Event&gt;)" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.os.VibrationEffect.Builder.addEvents</code>.</a></format></para>
